5,1,1,talk,George,,"I think we should be careful not to just fix the money, but the atmosphere. I'll look into what two other car-sharing households said and the spell of checking each other's figures.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I want to understand the actual time commitment involved in managing this. I'll look into the hours of use recorded in the diary and the month's trial of recording every run.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I am concerned about the practical reliability of the car on a daily basis. I will look into the state of the car at handover and the trips that repeat weekly.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I want to make sure we have a fair basis for splitting the costs. I'll look into last year's tax, insurance and parking papers, as well as last year's fuel receipts.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Minato,,I want to know how much we actually spend and who drives the most. I'll look into last year's fuel receipts and the hours of use recorded in the diary.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,George,,"It seems we have a good spread of interests. @Misaki and @Minato, you both chose the fuel receipts; perhaps you can compare notes later to see if the numbers align.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"Comparing notes is fine, but the data itself is what matters. I am more interested in the administrative burden. Let's see what the records actually reveal about our time.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with @Toshio. Data is useful, but the daily experience of using the car is what often causes the most friction. I hope the handover records shed some light on that.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"I agree that the daily experience matters, but without a clear understanding of the financial baseline, any new system might still feel unfair to some of us. I'll focus on the hard costs first.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Minato,,I think it's important to be fair to everyone. I'm curious to see if the numbers tell a different story than what we think. I hope we can all find a way to be happy.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,George,,"I appreciate the optimism, @Minato. However, let's remember that fairness isn't just about the math; it's about how we feel when we ask for the keys. I'm hoping the other households' experiences will guide us.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"Feelings are subjective, @George. I prefer to look at the hours spent coordinating. If the administrative cost is too high, no amount of ""good feelings"" will make the system sustainable in the long run.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"I understand your point, @Toshio, but a sustainable system also requires a car that is actually ready to drive. If the logistics are perfect but the car is empty or dirty, the system still fails.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"I see your points. However, if we ignore the financial imbalance, we risk creating a situation where some of us are quietly subsidizing others, which is its own kind of friction. We need a balanced view.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Minato,,I think everyone is saying something important. I'll listen carefully to what you all find. I just want us to be honest with each other so we can all feel comfortable using the car.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,George,,"Let's keep that honesty in mind. Since we have all selected our areas of investigation, I suggest we move forward and see what the evidence tells us. I look forward to hearing your findings.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Toshio,,Agreed. Let's proceed to the findings. I expect the data will clarify whether our current arrangement is a practical use of time or merely a source of inefficiency.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. I hope the information we gather allows us to address the actual points of failure in our daily routine, rather than just the theoretical ones. Let's see what we find.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Once we have the facts about the costs and usage, we can move toward a solution that is both practical and fair for everyone. Let's see what the records show.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Minato,,I'm excited to see what we find! I hope the information helps us understand each other better and makes everything easier for everyone. Let's go see the results!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
