60,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A seems too close to the bookkeeping that caused so much tension. Option B provides predictability and peace, but Option C might be too much of a burden on one person. I lean toward B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is exactly the administrative nightmare I warned about. Option C still requires per-trip coordination. Option B is the only choice that eliminates constant negotiation and bookkeeping. I vote for B.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option B is the most appealing to me. It guarantees that the car is available for those recurring weekly trips and removes the uncertainty of who is responsible for its state on a given day. I vote for B.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A is too much like the audit we want to avoid. Option C still leaves the financial split vague. Option B ensures a fair, fixed contribution and clear responsibility. I vote for B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I agree with everyone. Option B sounds the most peaceful because we won't have to worry about the money or the paperwork every single day. I want us all to be happy, so I vote for B!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,George,,"Since we are all in agreement, there is no need for further debate. Option B seems to be the most harmonious choice for our group. I'm glad we could reach a consensus so quickly.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
